+## 2026-09-02 — Induce-tier truncation: diagnosed, measured, partly fixed
+
+The ARC induction tier truncates mid-generation, making any tool A/B on the induce path
+uninterpretable. Root cause found, two fixes shipped, a truncation-free config sized.
+
+SHIPPED (committed):
+- Pool-truncation diagnostic was clipped before its numbers. `INDUCE_FAILURE_NOTE_CLIP`=500
+  now bounds all 5 induce-failure storage sites (was 4 independent clips 150/160/240/300 that
+  dropped the `RAISE -c` tail). REQ-ARC-WMTE-6860, mutation-proven. Commit 2c5d64ef25.
+- Env-gated `CARNOT_ARC_LLAMA_SERVER_PARALLEL` launch flag (unset -> 4-slot default, scored
+  path byte-identical; =1 -> one slot, whole pool). REQ-ARC-WMTE-6870, mutation-proven.
+  Commit b2cb725880. SECONDARY improvement, not the whole fix (see below).
+
+MECHANISM (directly measured, GPU 1, Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M, q8 KV):
+- The pool is UNIFIED: a single fresh stream owns all `-c` (a 15000-token generation completed
+  in full at `-c 49152`). Not divided into n_ctx/4.
+- The truncation is the induce PROMPT SIZE. `induce_prompt` renders every transition since
+  level-start (`k=None`); 82 transitions = 20431 tokens; live inductions carry 220-299.
+- Smoking gun: a 30010-token prompt on a single slot generated 19142 tokens then stopped
+  `stop=limit`, `truncated=true`, with prompt+gen = 30010+19142 = 49152 = EXACTLY the pool.
+  The generation hit the context wall, not the 26800 budget. So `--parallel 1` alone does NOT
+  fix it: a 30k prompt on one slot still caps generation near 19k.
+
+SIZED FIX (VRAM-verified on the 24 GB 3090, `--parallel 1`):
+- `-c 49152` -> 18183 MiB ; `-c 73728` -> 18858 MiB. Per-cell KV ~0.0275 MiB. Huge headroom.
+- Recommendation: set `CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX` to 98304 (MEASURED 19794 MiB, fits with ~4.5 GB headroom). Then even a 46k
+  prompt + 26800 budget (=72800) fits the pool, so the induce completes. No code change (the
+  knob exists). Capping transitions `k` is the deeper lever but is an accuracy A/B.
+
+NEXT (blocks the tool A/B, step 2):
+- Apply the sized `-c` (and optionally `--parallel 1`) to the eval, confirm a real induce
+  completes (reasoning_only falls, chars_final rises), THEN run the tool on/off A/B.
+- Supervisor evidence (step 3): the 14 unredirected windows/game do NOT yet specify a new arm
+  -- one curated arm (`tool_loop_reinduction`, gated by `CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM`) was
+  disabled, and the refinement contract needs ALL arms fired first. Enable it (step 2) before
+  declaring a new arm. Also: `resolved_by_levelup`/`helped` credit on transient live
+  level_progress (cd82: 0 banked levels, 3 redirects credited true), so they overcount success
+  -- use banked levels / actions-to-progress, never these counters.
